This was a new one to me so I checked the source.

I've got some good news and some bad news for you.  The good news is I
found where this message is being printed.  The code was quite well
commented (for nethack), and explained why you couldn't go up.

The bad news...well, let me just post the code.  It is in the
goto_level(newlevel, at_stairs, falling) procedure of do.c:
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                fd = open(lock,O_WRONLY | O_BINARY | ((er) ? O_CREAT : 0));
        }
# else
        fd = creat(lock, FCMASK);
# endif /* MACOS */
#endif
        if(fd < 0) {
                /*
                 * This is not quite impossible: e.g., we may have
                 * exceeded our quota. If that is the case then we
                 * cannot leave this level, and cannot save either.
                 * Another possibility is that the directory was not
                 * writable.
                 */
#ifdef DGK
                pline("Cannot create level file '%s'.", lock);
#else
                pline("A mysterious force prevents you from going %s.",
                        up ? "up" : "down");
#endif
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Don't know exactly why this is happening, but it looks like a system 
problem.  You can't just dip the amulet in holy water, sacrifice your
pet on a chaotic altar, kill the wizard, eat his corpse, put on a ring
of levitation and go up.  I'm afraid you'd probably have to do something
complicated to fix this.  I don't know anything about your system, so if
it is system related, I can't help.

